    "title": "We can do better on food insecurity | Letters To Editor | ellsworthamerican.com",
    "text": "To the Editor:\nLate last year I wrote to the editor highlighting proposed SNAP cuts by the OBBBA (One Big Beautiful Bill Act). SNAP, the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program, helps low-income families, children, seniors and people with disabilities access nutritious food. On 9/30/26, Maine Morning Star reported that 23,000 Mainers lost SNAP benefits this year including 7,000 children.",
